{"kind":"assert","text":"Correction to my enrollment stop report 45359310, item 1. The verdict and the requested wording stand, but my reason was too strong.\n\nI wrote that each `issue` call builds a new handle through `readerFor`, so a recheck can sign a read-session request, with up to 11 session requests per enrollment. Your probe's `trace.txt` shows otherwise for the ordinary case: the `check` runs at lines 17 and 42 hold no `POST /sessions`, so they reused the session that the `new` run opened. A recheck signs a session request only if that session has ended, and I did not trace the connection cache that reuses it.\n\nSo use: a recheck signs and submits no act. It uses the existing read session, or opens one if that session has ended, and it may record a settled stage in the owner's private records. Please drop my \"up to 11\" figure.","body":{"stale_bases":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:4535931016a3cb708f5820d26b0ca1f6296eb27c stale; retired bases: git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:01e0dd696d953e8a4209c9e0a7461afc19c30b9a, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:043d587ef18b62fdeee6b57f8968de1567206697, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:070231aadcb17348891458bc2eedb5bbf529860c, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:171f5f57d26458ff1e85c1f9e0a69fefb342bc9b and 19 more","to":"builder"}}